SUMMARY:Rattlesnake Lodge to Folk Art Center along the MST  10 miles\, 140
 0' elevation
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Meeting Spot**: Folk Art Center 
 on the Blue Ridge Parkway. Prompt 8:30 departure\n**Description**: This is
  a point to point hike. We will meet at the Folk Art Center and shuttle up
  to the Rattle Snake Lodge starting point. Follow the MST Trail from the r
 emnants of the Rattlesnake Lodge\, a turn of the century lodge built by an
  Asheville physician\, to the Folk Art Center. There is a large variety of
  colorful wildflowers along the trail\, which is mostly downhill with a fe
 w short climbs. There is a nice overlook for a lunch/snack break. Good foo
 ting. Shaded. Pace: 2.4 mph. Dogs welcome if on a leash. A lunch spot afte
 r the hike would be nice--suggestions welcome\n\n**Courtesy\, (Please Abid
 e!)**\n\n**Only sign up if you \\*truly\\* plan to come.** If you must can
 cel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid 
 dropping out within 24 hours of the hike so wait-listers can have sufficie
 nt notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n**LEGALESE**\nThi
 s Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transporta
 tion to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their o
 wn safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical cond
 itioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself a
 nd property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can as
 sure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full respons
 ibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315504124
 /
